# An assignment is `{ __v = value; place op= __v }` (INTERNALS
# "Assignments"). Liveness is textual, so a later arm's guard keeps the
# subject's view live in an earlier arm, and a view re-pointed by the
# assignment keeps its old loan through the value. A reassigned owner's
# old value is dropped after the value: a `drop` that reads a slice of a
# Vec the value grew reads freed memory, which the oracle does not model.
